Recursion #4 -- Current

ALGORITHM
- Build each sequence one marble at a time, tracking used colours in a bitmask.
- At each position, try every unused single colour, then every unused pair (i < j,
  so "blue+green" is never also produced as "green+blue").
- Do one pass per marble count (1..N) so output is grouped like the README sample.
- No permutations, no duplicates, no filtering, and sequences stream straight to stdout.
- Rewritten in Swift (Package.swift, Sources/, Tests/). The Java/Eclipse version was removed.

RESULT
- Fixes #3, which missed sequences with more than one two-colour marble
  (e.g. "blue+green red+yellow"). Counts for 1..8:
  1, 5, 24, 136, 935, 7671, 73360, 801704
- Work is proportional to the output size (~800k lines for 8 colours), so 8 colours takes seconds, not hours.
